<title>HONG KONG: HKCB Bank 1996 net rises 10.95 percent.</title>
<headline>HKCB Bank 1996 net rises 10.95 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   24.8	 vs 22.2</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    10.0	 vs 9.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  24.62 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    147.31     vs 132.77</p>
<p>    Company name		 HKCB Bank Holding Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 17-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 17</p>
<p>NOTE - HKCB Bank is the local banking unit of Lippo Ltd.</p>
<p>The exceptional item represents partial provision for the premium which may become payable on December 8, 1997, in the event that Swiss Francs 65 million redeemable convertible notes issued by a subsidiary are redeemed by the noteholders.</p>
<p>Based on the company's current share price, the directors are of the opinion that it would be prudent to provide 50 percent of the premium amount given the possibility that the notes may be redeemed rather than being converted.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 15 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of five cents) vs 14 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
